# Windsurf Cascade Rules for Remotion 3D Skill

## Project Overview
This repository contains a Standalone Universal Multi-Agent Skill for composing deterministic 3D animation scenes in Remotion using Three.js and React Three Fiber.

## Prime Directive: Deterministic Rendering
- NEVER use real-time or asynchronous clocks (`Date.now()`, `Clock.getDelta()`, `requestAnimationFrame()`, `setTimeout`).
- All 3D movement and shaders MUST be pure deterministic functions of Remotion's `frame` and `fps`.
- Use Remotion's native `spring` and `interpolate` utilities.

## Asset Workflow
- Available 3D assets are cataloged in `references/asset-catalog.md`.
- Inspect components via CLI: `npm run list-assets` (or `npx tsx scripts/list-assets.ts`).
- Scaffold scenes & inject self-contained component templates:
  ```bash
  npx tsx scripts/scaffold-scene.ts --name=<SceneName> --template=diorama-explainer --inject
  ```
- Target project dependencies required: `npm install three @react-three/fiber @remotion/three zod`.
